1. Audit Purpose

This independent, non-repairing audit verifies the closed G2-B1 through G2-B6 implementation against the committed v0.1.1 preflight. It authorizes internal closure evidence only and changes no runtime, test, demo, schema, release, or specification.

2. Audited Committed Basis

The audited immutable implementation basis is HEAD 58167e022f77b53550e65df2f5b1ff1cdc154eee on main, equal to origin/main, with an initially clean worktree and empty staging.
The binding preflight is revision v0.1.1 with SHA-256 0b72a7794c0eee9d86d7745a304f7c4341d3e2c8b7ffece3665f16e38643a094.

3. Ordered Commit Ancestry

- b78183b3bd5ecc5e9ea2201b9fe498d208423747 - Close G2-A ActionPacket lifecycle and kill-switch
- 3364aba6ac5c2141f7737b43b5b8a153827f947a - Add G2-B semantic address and reuse preflight
- ad81b0a3ef82d85662e3b2c494e39b91ea19566d - Correct G2-B preflight identity framing
- 8a6c6d9f4ada81238892c5b58f534375824ff6ef - Implement G2-B1 canonical DRS contracts and schemas
- 86ecc3543f72d9d8e7d59a8ae9813fd882871fe7 - Implement G2-B2 temporal eligibility and ranking
- bf5d57210c5126cf4f3ebe59525ef5066814ca88 - Implement G2-B3 Root-approved controlled memory descent
- ee6ccbb50188520bb88e29bcfecaf85c331d9360 - Implement G2-B4 Root-bound informational shortcut
- 4e806369f213f6746b62c2bcb308a4eed0f33527 - Implement G2-B5 pure local adapter and immutable writeback
- 58167e022f77b53550e65df2f5b1ff1cdc154eee - Integrate G2-B6 Living Gauntlet and Kernel Conformance

Every commit exists, each is an ancestor of the next, and the reverse rev-list from G2-A closure through G2-B6 contains exactly the eight ordered G2-B commits.

4. Exact Commit and Path-Scope Verification

All eight G2-B commits match their exact authorized path sets. The inclusive unique path set contains exactly 20 paths. There is no deletion, rename, inserted commit, foreign path, release edit, README edit, specification edit, provider edit, connector edit, or public release/RC2 path.

5. Frozen G2-A and Release Boundary

G2-A remains CLOSED_PASS at closure commit b78183b3bd5ecc5e9ea2201b9fe498d208423747. All 13 dedicated G2-A implementation/test/runner/preflight/audit/checkpoint paths match their closure bytes. Shared Living and Conformance paths preserve executable v1.0/v1.1 and v0.1/v0.2 historical geometries.
release/completion_manifest.json and release/integration_seam_index.json match their frozen hashes. Gate 2, public release, RC2, and G2-C remain unclaimed.

6. Canonical Family, Public Surface, and Exact-Type Findings

Exactly one canonical G2-B family exists with 19 frozen dataclasses. Every field tuple, builder, validator, serializer, evaluator, ranker, descent function, Root shortcut validator, B5 collector/total validator, and Living act matches the preflight surface. Exact built-in types, bool/int separation, subclass resistance, deterministic serializers, and total validation are executable.

7. Semantic Address, Time, Query, and Lifecycle Findings

The seven-field address material, drsaddr_v01 identity, bounded namespace, signed-int64 time, explicit evaluation source, half-open validity/TTL, six ordered query modes, immutable query evaluation, and six persistent lifecycle states all pass.

8. Pointer, Secret, Read-Purity, and Compatibility Findings

MeaningRecord carries no dense payload. Pointer storage classes and access policy are exact; no pointer creates authority. Raw secrets are rejected. Legacy projections remain context-only evidence. The pure reader calls neither LocalDRS.layer_path nor mutation methods, and hedgehog/drs.py remains frozen.

9. Eligibility, Ranking, and Resolution Findings

All hard eligibility gates execute before ranking. Ranking receives eligible candidates only, uses signed integer units and exact weights, ends ties with canonical candidate ID, and cannot turn score, GT, freshness, similarity, or lineage into authority.

10. Root-Approved Descent and Accounting Findings

RetrievalPlan is proposal-only. The seven-counter budget is bounded, Root may narrow but not expand it, SUMMARY_ONLY opens zero payload bytes, OPEN_ONE_ARTIFACT is bounded, and observed pointer/record/artifact/byte/edge/conflict/depth accounting is exact with zero effects.

11. Root Shortcut and ReuseCertificate Findings

RootDecisionKernelV01 remains the sole shortcut authority. Root input, result, owner, candidate, query, scope, and hashes cross-bind exactly. ReuseCertificate has complete identity/use-time checks and creates no authority, permission, FinalOutput, packet, receipt, capability, effect handle, effect, truth, or action proof.

12. G2-A History and Action-Reuse Fence Findings

All eight action-shaped requests fail closed. Expired, revoked, superseded, blocked, failed, consumed, uncertain-closed, receipt, prior-permission, and prior-Root-Final history remains evidence only and cannot authorize reuse.

13. Immutable Writeback and Supersession Findings

The shared pure writeback-geometry validator binds exact Root transaction, owner, accepted result, claim, unique claim_dimension tag, predecessor, successor commitment, canonical edge, and successor. One immutable successor is written per success, predecessor bytes remain unchanged, and failed writeback leaves no partial successor.

14. Two-Domain Deterministic Proof Findings

TRAVEL_POLICY_INFORMATION and WAREHOUSE_MAINTENANCE_INFORMATION use the same generic contract. Both prove pointer-first SUMMARY_ONLY descent, ANSWER_SHORTCUT, context fallback, immutable successor writeback, predecessor preservation, and zero effects.

